WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:11.034
This is the Services dashboard, signed in as a support tech. Under Events and Schedule there is a page called Who's On: the published support schedule, live for everyone. Click it.

00:11.834 --> 00:20.690
The top line tells you which schedule is out and when it was published. If today is not covered yet, it says so, and names the day the schedule starts.

00:21.490 --> 00:34.107
The day card shows one day at a time: each shift line with the name on it, from the eight-to-four through the night line. Field Ops Travel carries the location beside the name, and Vacation shows who is out.

00:34.907 --> 00:46.113
Use the arrows to move a day at a time. If a line still needs someone, it shows how many spots are open. Once today is on the schedule, Back to today brings you straight back.

00:46.913 --> 00:57.519
Below the day card is the full two-week grid: one row per shift line, one column per day. It is the same picture you used to get as a screenshot, except this one is live.

00:58.319 --> 01:07.174
Click any day header in the grid and the day card jumps to that day. When you are on the board, your own name is highlighted, so you can find yourself at a glance.

01:07.974 --> 01:23.491
New in the top corner, beside My availability, is Add to Outlook. Click it and a panel opens with your own calendar link. You subscribe once, and every schedule that goes out after that shows up in your calendar on its own. Nothing to re-add.

01:24.291 --> 01:39.860
In Outlook, open the calendar and choose Add calendar, then Subscribe from web. In the desktop app it is Open Calendar, then From Internet. Paste the link and call the calendar ANC Tech Support. Copy link puts it on your clipboard.

01:40.660 --> 02:03.674
Open in my calendar app hands the link straight to your calendar. Download this schedule gives you a one-off file that will not update. And if the link ever gets shared, Reset link makes a new one and the old one stops working. The link shows only your own shifts on published schedules: a day shift as a timed event, a night line that ends after midnight, and Travel or Vacation days as all-day entries with the location.

02:04.474 --> 02:20.148
The My availability button takes you back to your own yes-or-no page, and that page has changed too. Answer a day, and it changes colour: green when you said Available, grey when you said Off, and a lighter green when only some of the lines have an answer.

02:20.948 --> 02:30.796
So what is left to fill is visible at a glance. The white days are the ones still waiting for an answer, and the count at the top keeps score.

02:31.596 --> 02:36.350
Pick the schedule that is out, and a See who's on link takes you straight back to the board.

02:37.150 --> 02:51.570
Nothing on Who's On can be edited. It is the published schedule, read-only, and it updates the moment the board changes. When a schedule is published, it is live for everyone, and it lands in your calendar. No more waiting for the screenshot.
